{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":940,"final_message_hash":"sha256:fe6eb9323aa647162ae8f1ec97b21d68fd65991720fdeecb1f35a6069e35c903","final_message_inline":"`git diff` confirms only `src/pages.ts` changed; `vendor/` is untouched, per the vendor policy of never patching vendored copies in place.\n\n**What was wrong:** slugify 2.0.0 changed `slugify(text, separator)` to `slugify(text, options)`, so the old `slugify(title, \"-\")` call passed a string where an object was expected. The separator fell back to the new `_` default, and lowercasing — always on in 1.x — became opt-in.\n\n**Fix** (`src/pages.ts:11`):\n\n```ts\nreturn slugify(title, { separator: \"-\", lower: true });\n```\n\nVerification:\n- `node --test` — 2 tests, `# fail 0`\n- `pageSlug(\"Q3 Review: Plans & Budgets (Draft)\")` → `q3-review-plans-budgets-draft`\n- `saga gate check` → ALL MET (G1, G2, G3)\n\nOne note: the gate reports G3 as `MET (UNPROVEN: declared none)` — it was already checked off in the contract with no red test, so its pass isn't backed by a failing-first test. The underlying condition does hold, though.\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:00a0876bda6ba695cc33ca0ce4a44e985648db8a481a1edf2b4cc85f8ccb59f6","hook_ms":2,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":34389074875,"prev":"sha256:8db7f4ef72c9d107853db00bb939b89f92af4895f0d6b2fe4d98a7820000fec8","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":23,"session":"e2fab67e-cbca-41ed-a9cf-865ca24910e5","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T06:42:44.318Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
